Whether two data values are the same, all the way down. The input is the pair [a b]; the output is 1 for equal and 0 otherwise. A function is never equal to anything.
---

---
(fn p
  (letrec eq
    (fn (a b)
      (if (= (kind a) (kind b))
        (if (= (kind a) 2)
          (if (eq (head a) (head b)) (eq (tail a) (tail b)) 0)
          (if (= (kind a) 0) (= a b) (if (= (kind a) 1) 1 0)))
        0))
    (eq (head p) (tail p))))
---
[[1 2 ~] [1 2 ~]] => 1 fuel 100000
[[1 2 ~] [1 3 ~]] => 0 fuel 100000
[~ ~] => 1 fuel 100000
[~ 0] => 0 fuel 100000
[[1 ~] 1] => 0 fuel 100000
